Limits violation protection

The BMS shall detect any violation on any cell of the pack and react as fast as possible to protect the batteries.
The BMS shall have a strong focus and monitor the cell voltages and temperatures at any given time and be able to reach by either opening the contactor and/or reducing the power limits.

Inputs:
cell voltage fast filtered
cell temperature fast filtered

Outputs:
Contactor Immediate Opening Request
Critical error flag

Parameters:
V_crit_min, V_crit_max (2.3V - 3.8V)
T_crit_min, T_crit_max (0, 45 degC)

1. Cell voltage limits:
a. If any of the cell voltage (fast filtered) goes above V_crit_max, the BMS shall immediately open all the contactors. Then the BMS shall throw a critical error.
b. If any of the cell voltage (fast filtered) goes below V_crit_min, the BMS shall immediately open all the contactors. Then the BMS shall throw a critical error.

2. Cell temperature limits:
a. If any of the cell temperature (fast filtered) goes above T_crit_max, the BMS shall immediately open all the contactors. Then the BMS shall throw a critical error.
b. If any of the cell temperature (fast filtered) goes below T_crit_min, the BMS shall immediately open all the contactors. Then the BMS shall throw a critical error.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TESTING
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Testing cell limit violations implies testing the function with fake limits in order not to damage the cells.

1. Voltage limits:

a. High limit:
Bring the cell voltage to 3-3.2V for example.
Set the parameters V_crit_max to 3.5V.
Charge the cell until it reaches 3.5V (safe).
Note: make sure the current is low (<10A) when crossing the new V_crit_max V in order to avoid damaging the contactors.
-> Observe: The contactors should open immediately upon crossing V_crit_max.

b. Low limit:
Bring the cell voltage to 3-3.2V for example.
Set the parameters V_crit_min to 2.9V.
Discharge the cell until it crosses 2.9V (safe).
Note: make sure the current is low (<10A) when crossing the new V_crit_min V in order to avoid damaging the contactors.
-> Observe: The contactors should open immediately upon crossing V_crit_min.

2. Temperature limits:
Apply the same principle as above: change the T_crit_min and T_crit_max limits to values as close as possible to the actual cell temperature value.
Play with the temperature sensor itself (NTC) to trigger a critical error for both min and max temperature limits.
-> Observe: In both case the contactors should open immediately upon crossing T_crit_min and T_crit_max.

